    {
        "content": "<p>I'm still not sure what you mean by \"decision procedures for automata\".  The example you gave looks like a very specific type of the model checking problem: reachability.  Even here, you would want to solve the more general problem of whether a set of states is reachable, not just a single target state.  But there are other types of model checking problems beyond reachability as well.  Indeed, there is a vast literature on model checking  (including several textbooks) and many existing model checkers whose performance will probably beat any simple implementation in Lean.  So, before your questions can be adequately answered, I think you need to elaborate more on what type of model checking problems you want to solve and what techniques you would like to use in your solver.</p>",
        "id": 626708745,
        "sender_full_name": "Ching-Tsun Chou",
        "timestamp": 1790276793
    }
]